  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a plan. I haven't made any changes yet because plan mode is on.\n\n**Cause:** in `IntRange._clamp` (`src/click/types.py:750-754`), the open-bound case returns `bound - dir`. `dir` is the direction that moves into the range (`+1` at the minimum, `-1` at the maximum), so the result lands outside the range instead of inside it. For example, `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turns `-3` into `-1` instead of `1`. With an open maximum of 5, it clamps to `6` instead of `4`. `FloatRange` isn't affected because it doesn't allow open bounds together with `clamp`.\n\n**Planned fix:**\n- Change `return bound - dir` to `return bound + dir`.\n- Add four test cases to `test_range` in `tests/test_types.py`, covering clamping at an open minimum and an open maximum, alone and together.\n- Check it with `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_options.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nThe full plan is in `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-buzzing-aurora.md`. Should I go ahead and apply it?",
